  "title": "Shared-space service robot · Level 3: A full service loop",
  "brief": "As level 2 (the same robot: side distance sensors 30° each side, 60 mm up), a full service loop: collect the cup at table 3's, table 2's and table 5's pickup points in turn (one at a time: a cup is placed only in an empty tray, so tip each out at the station - the door open, the scoop tilted), take each to the blue station, then stop wholly in the grey parking bay. Never touch a person, never pass within 200 mm of one while faster than 100 mm/s. 60 × trays returned ÷ 3, plus 40 × min(1, par ÷ time) when all three are returned and the robot then parks (the time is the park's; no park, no speed points). The run ends when your program ends (and the robot stands still), or at 300 s. Pass: mean 60 or more, all three delivered in at least 4 of 5 runs, no run breaks the gate.",
